Subject: Do not download a cluster-matched kubectl at runtime on the 2.17 line

Origin: DHI-internal (runtime dependency policy)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/kubeflow/pipelines a0733cb51b0484a6050cafee989ffe3312f808ad
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/kubeflow-pipelines-cache-deployer/tests -run TestClosureRoot -count=1` expect "ok"
Forwarded: no (upstream offers no switch to turn the download off)
Drop-When: never: upstream calls the download unconditionally; revisit if upstream adds a way to turn it off

The 2.17.3 deployer downloads a kubectl matching the API server into $HOME/bin before it
talks to the cluster. Its download block is inline rather than the function that 2.18.0 uses,
so the 2.17 line carries this patch instead of disable-runtime-kubectl-download.patch. The
package declares the pinned kubectl-1.36 line as a runtime dependency, so a running deployer
never executes a binary it fetched itself and needs neither curl nor jq for that step. The
block is removed whole, including the PATH change it makes, so the packaged kubectl is the
only kubectl on PATH.

--- a/backend/src/cache/deployer/deploy-cache-service.sh
+++ b/backend/src/cache/deployer/deploy-cache-service.sh
@@ -28,18 +28,6 @@
 MUTATING_WEBHOOK_CONFIGURATION_NAME="cache-webhook-${NAMESPACE}"
 WEBHOOK_SECRET_NAME=webhook-server-tls

-# Getting correct kubectl. Kubernetes only supports kubectl versions within +/-1 minor version.
-# kubectl has some resource version information hardcoded, so using too old kubectl can lead to errors
-mkdir -p "$HOME/bin"
-export PATH="$HOME/bin:$PATH"
-{
-    server_version_major_minor=$(kubectl version --output json | jq --raw-output '(.serverVersion.major + "." + .serverVersion.minor)' | tr -d '"+')
-    stable_build_version=$(curl -fsSL "https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable-${server_version_major_minor}.txt")
-    kubectl_url="https://dl.k8s.io/release/${stable_build_version}/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"
-    curl -L -o "$HOME/bin/kubectl" "$kubectl_url"
-    chmod +x "$HOME/bin/kubectl"
-} || true
-
 # This should fail if there are connectivity problems
 # Gotcha: Listing all objects requires list permission,
 # but when listing a single oblect kubectl will fail if it's not found
